            "id": 12,
            "name": "Artisan Sourdough Loaf",
            "short_description": "Our signature sourdough is fermented for 48 hours to achieve the perfect tangy flavor, a caramelized crust, and a soft, airy interior. Perfect for sandwiches or dipping in soup.",
            "description": "<p>Experience the authentic taste of traditional baking with our Artisan Sourdough Loaf. Made with just three simple ingredients—flour, water, and salt—and our 10-year-old starter culture.</p><p><strong>The Process:</strong> We use a slow-fermentation process that lasts over 48 hours. This breaks down the gluten, making it easier to digest, while developing a complex, rich flavor profile that commercial breads simply cannot match.</p><p><strong>Tasting Notes:</strong> Expect a thick, crunchy crust that protects a moist, open-crumb interior. The flavor is mildly tangy with nutty undertones.</p><p><strong>Serving Suggestions:</strong> excellent toasted with butter, perfect for avocado toast, or as a side to a hearty beef stew.</p>",
